    "narrative": "Today\u2019s landscape for the Austin Waves is limited as we navigate the tail end of the season, leaving **Liam Hicks** as our primary focal point in the catcher slot. His 46.06 daily efficiency score is fueled by a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against May (R), which offsets the 6% park penalty to keep him in the \"Marginal\" start category. While the scarcity of high-impact offensive production today limits our ceiling, **Liam Hicks** remains the lone active rostered player to clear our internal threshold for engagement, positioned in the heart of the order at #4 to maximize RBI potential despite a pedestrian 3.99 SP_xERA for the opposition.\n\nThe decision-making process for the bench was largely dictated by the league-wide schedule, as heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are sidelined by an off-day, alongside **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Andy Pages**. We continue to monitor the utility roles held by **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, and **Jacob Wilson** to ensure our game cap management remains disciplined. While **Heliot Ramos** and **Nasim Nunez** remain high-priority assets due to their speed profile\u2014crucial for our pursuit of the stolen base category\u2014their lack of a matchup today means they join **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias** in storage. No weather-related risks are currently flagged for the limited slate, but the lack of depth on today's active schedule reinforces the necessity of preserving our remaining daily starts for more favorable statistical environments later this week.",
